  "description": "This program prepares candidates to teach in special education settings. Candidates earn the K-12 Cognitive Impairment endorsement on the Michigan teaching certificate. Unlike the Special Education K-12 Major: Cognitive Impairment, BA, program, this program requires candidates to complete another certifiable major or minor. Candidates choose one student-teaching option: Complete one semester of student teaching in both special- and general-education settings (EDUC 346). Complete two semesters of student teaching with one semester in general education (EDUC 346) and one semester in special education (EDUC 347). If combined with the elementary education birth-kindergarten major, complete one semester of student teaching in special education (EDUC 347).",
